From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arr-optimized <arr-optimized@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Optimize settings page: every optimization value
 adjustable, live, with status

Adds Settings > Optimize (/settings/optimize), GET/PUT /api/v3/config/optimize,
GET /api/v3/config/optimize/settings and GET /api/v3/config/optimize/status.

- Main settings: indexer request spacing (0-10000 ms, empty = stock 2000 ms),
  cache hit header/value, ffprobe timeout (0-1440 min, default 15, 0 = none).
- Advanced tuning: grab spacing, custom-format cache entries/expiry/max input
  length, per-search indexer memo, release profile cache, and every ffprobe
  cache limit (entries, MB, max result KB, failure/idle/recently-written
  lifetimes, settle time, sweep interval), each with bounds, a warning range
  and Reset to default.
- Values are stored in the Config table ("optimize..." keys). A valid
  ARR_* environment variable wins and locks the field (PUT ignores it);
  otherwise the saved value; otherwise the default. Invalid values -> 400
  with field errors (numbers are long, so too-large numbers get the same
  field error). PUT changes only the values it carries (missing/null =
  unchanged, like the other config endpoints); the default value resets.
- OptimizeSettings is an immutable snapshot swapped on Save/ConfigSavedEvent;
  hot paths do one volatile read. Cache limits apply at once under each
  cache's own lock; 0 turns a cache off and takes the uncached path.
- Defaults equal the previous constants (stock timing, same caches), except
  the ffprobe timeout default, which rises from 5 to 15 minutes.
- Status: built-in optimizations and Interlocked counters (CF cache,
  ffprobe cache, ffprobe timeouts, cache-hit refunds, paced waits).
- The settings list shows the value in effect (max ffprobe result size is
  capped by the cache memory limit, with a note).
- UI: number fields carry the API bounds; a 400 that is not a list of field
  errors is shown as an error instead of breaking the page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
